  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This would mainly be useful for detecting when an object's owner leaves a world, but could have other applications for role-based transfers and mutually exclusive role acquisition.\n\nThe primary use case for this is to make dynamically spawned objects that automatically despawn when their owner leaves. Currently, the only other way to accomplish this is to have a watchdog timer that constantly broadcasts the owner's presence across the network to keep the object alive. This is less than ideal as it needlessly floods the network with messages the more of these objects get spawned and suffers from premature deletion should a hiccup in the network prevent the watchdog event from being propagated before timeout.\n\nAn OnOnwershipTransferred trigger would trigger for both the old owner and the new owner when an ownership transfer occurs and would allow objects to detect when they get transferred to a new owner allowing them to react appropriately should their current owner leave.",
